module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.rest_success_and_decode_are_separately_true

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data rest_success_and_decode_are_separately_true: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "rest_success_and_decode_are_separately_true" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "REST success and REST decode are separately true and only one of them is checked (an operation is declared, hermetically witnessed and green while its LIVE decode path has never produced a value; the outcome classifies as SUCCESS because a 200 did come back, and the decoded record is Null, so a consumer reads a successful fetch that fetched nothing)",
    "FOUND 2026-09-10 BY A PROBE THAT WAS BUILT TO ANSWER A DIFFERENT QUESTION, on gunbc#10964. A review asked for the GitHub contents API's `size` field to be typed as a std.measure ByteSize rather than a bare Int. Shipping that on a hermetic green was refusable on its face - a mock_response is authored .dag data - so the live path was run instead, with a real token, at the exact ref the change's own fixture names: GET https://api.github.com/repos/biomejs/biome/contents/.github/workflows/main.yml at 47d7383d049b36ff8eaba50912176928143dd9e9. It refused inside the classifier with TypeError \"cannot access field 'encoding' on Null\". ",
    "THREE NEGATIVE CONTROLS, RECORDED SO THE NEXT READER DOES NOT RE-RUN THEM. (1) Reverting the field to `size: Int` does not change it, which rules out the Measure. (2) A throwaway operation whose entire response type is a single `sha: String` does not change it, which rules out field-set strictness against a response body carrying a dozen fields the record does not name. (3) The outcome classified as RestExchangeSucceeded rather than a transport arm, which rules out a network or credential failure and fixes the state precisely: the request was made, a 200 came back, and the body did not become the declared record. ",
    "WHAT MAKES THIS GREEN-FOR-THE-WRONG-REASON RATHER THAN MERELY UNDER-COVERED, which is the distinguishing fact and the whole reason it earns a row. A mock_response NEVER PASSES THROUGH THE WIRE DECODER: it is authored .dag data published beside the operation and substituted for the exchange. So the hermetic witness and this defect are DISJOINT - not a weak test of the right thing, but a correct test of a different thing. No amount of strengthening the hermetic claims can reach it, and every strengthening makes the coverage look better. ",
    "THE BLAST RADIUS IS EVERY EFFECTFUL REST CONSUMER, and on the evidence available at this writing NO live REST read has passing evidence anywhere in this corpus. gunbc.github_authenticated_user_read is the only other live-capable consumer and its own annotation states that live GET /user is not executed in the change that added it. gunbc#10923 landed the performer these all sit on under the title \"Give GitHubEffect a REST performer whose shape is hermetically verdicted\" - shape-verdicted and live-unexercised is exactly this gap, and it is cited here so the next reader does not assume that change covered it. ",
    "RUNG AND CEILING. Found at MITIGATABLE AT BEST: the failure is loud when a consumer touches a field, and silent for any consumer that does not - a fold over a decoded list would see an empty list and report a repository with no matching workflow, which is a fabricated observation arriving through the success path. The ceiling is a live-path probe enrolled as executing evidence beside the hermetic ones, and the NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER is that probe existing: one operation, one real credential, one asserted decoded field, run where a required lane can see it. Until it exists, a hermetic green on a REST operation establishes the SHAPE of its response and says nothing about whether the wire produces one. ",
    "THE REVIEW TELL IS A MOCK STANDING WHERE A DECODE WAS NEVER OBSERVED: an operation whose only executed evidence is a mock_response, and a PR body that describes what the endpoint returns without a receipt showing the endpoint's bytes becoming the declared value. The authoring tell is the one that produced this row - reaching for a live run because a hermetic green would not have settled the question being asked. ",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
